    {
      "id": "628161",
      "text": "The generation recipe is:\n\nCompute SHA256(tensor_name.encode()).\nInterpret the first eight digest bytes as an unsigned big-endian integer.\nUse that integer to seed NumPy’s PCG64 generator.\nGenerate standard_normal(shape, dtype=np.float32).\nApply:\nNormalization weights: exp(float32(0.06) * z)\nConvolution kernels: z * float32(1/6)\nConvert to BF16 using round-to-nearest, ties-to-even.\nAfter identifying these recipes, predictions were recorded for 21 previously unread tensors, containing 423,168 values. Every predicted value matched the subsequent HTTP Range reads exactly. A separate verification script then fetched all 43 tensors again and confirmed the same byte-for-byte matches.",
      "time": "00:44",
      "sender_name": "Baicai iaciaB",
      "sender_id": 8833475412
    },
